ty and auditory or visual awareness of each child?s on going activity (26 TAC §746.1205(a)(4))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1362029-i20240808-v4","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-631-b","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1362029-i20240808","date":"2024-08-08","original_code":"746.631(b)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-09-13","finding":"Caregivers Have Access to Tracking System: During a DFPS investigation, the caregivers did not have a tracking system to determine which children were in care. A child who wandered away from the operation was not signed in for the day.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026635296","violation_type_title":"Caregivers Have Access to Tracking System (26 TAC §746.631(b))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1362029-i20240808-v5","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-307-b-4","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1362029-i20240808","date":"2024-08-08","original_code":"746.307(b)(4)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-09-13","finding":"Parental Communication - Situation that Placed a Child at Risk: During a DFPS investigation, it was determined that a child was left outside in the playground and proceeded to  wander away from the operation. The operation did not notify the parent immediately, as required.  When the parent picked up their child that day, the operation still failed to notify them of the incident.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026635295","violation_type_title":"Parental Communication - Situation that Placed a Child at Risk (26 TAC §746.307(b)(4))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"}]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1362029-i20240711","date":"2024-07-11","inspection_type":"Inspection","result":"No deficiencies cited","passed":true,"violation_count":0,"open_count":0,"evidence_class":"VERIFIED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","sourc